Package: netmatchRI
Title: Dual-Penalty Matching and Randomization-Based Inference
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Zhejia", "Dong", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "zhejia_dong@brown.edu")
Author: Zhejia Dong [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Zhejia Dong <zhejia_dong@brown.edu>
Description: Implements dual-penalty matching and randomization-based inference
    for observational network data with network dependence and interference.
    The dual-penalty matched design incorporates network proximity across
    treatment arms and among units assigned to the same matched sets. It also
    includes comparison matching designs, design-based variance bounds,
    sensitivity analysis, critical sensitivity curves, and a built-in 300-unit
    example dataset. An optional interface to the commercial 'Gurobi Optimizer'
    is available. Eligible academic users can request a free license at
    <https://www.gurobi.com/academics/>. The optimizer can be downloaded from
    <https://www.gurobi.com/product/download-center>. The associated 'gurobi'
    R package is not available from CRAN; it is distributed with the optimizer
    and can be installed by following the official instructions at
    <https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/reference/r/setup.html>.
